  "question": {
    "text": "The molarity of the solution prepared by dissolving <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of oxalic acid <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>250</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math> of water in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>mol</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is _________ . (Nearest integer)<br />[Atomic mass : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>]",
